  "description": "The INVALID SELECTOR arm at app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl:196-202, whose value is not the message it paints but the early exit it does NOT take. 'X' is typed into the second selection cell, so the ten-way EVALUATE TRUE at :148 stops at its SECOND arm: :152 tests presence only - NOT = SPACES AND LOW-VALUES - so any non-blank byte selects a row and only the inner EVALUATE ever judges it, and :153-154 move 'X' into CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SEL-FLG and the row-two identifier 0000000000000022 into CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SELECTED. Both conjuncts of :183-184 are therefore true, and the EVALUATE at :185 falls past WHEN 'S' (:186) and WHEN 's' (:187) into WHEN OTHER (:196), which is last as gate G30 requires. TWO STATEMENTS IN THAT ARM ARE COMMENTED OUT IN THE SOURCE - :197 '* SET TRANSACT-EOF TO TRUE' and :202 '* PERFORM SEND-TRNLST-SCREEN' - and nothing in the arm sets WS-ERR-FLG either, which is exactly what the non-numeric TRNIDINI arm at :212 does do. With no error flag, no end of file, no send, no XCTL and no GO TO, execution FALLS STRAIGHT THROUGH :203-204 into the rest of PROCESS-ENTER-KEY: TRNIDINI is spaces so :206-207 positions the browse at LOW-VALUES, :221 repositions the cursor, :224 resets the page number from the three it arrived with to zero, and :225 paints a FULL ten-row page - :285 is false because the AID is ENTER so there is no skip read, :290-292 blanks the ten row slots, :297-303 fills them with records 1 to 10 stepping WS-IDX at :301, :305 is true so :306-307 computes 0 + 1 = 1, and the look-ahead READNEXT at :308 finds record 11 and reaches :310 SET NEXT-PAGE-YES. The single send is :326's, and WS-MESSAGE still holds the invalid-selection text, so the terminal shows a fully populated page one AND an error line at the same time. That combination is this case's signature: an implementation that returned early on an invalid selector would paint an empty page and fail here. :227-229 then runs too, because ERR-FLG-ON is false, so TRNIDINO is blanked twice - at :325 and again at :228. The two commented statements must stay no-ops and the absent WS-ERR-FLG assignment must stay absent (practice B5): restoring either would be a behaviour change dressed up as a tidy-up. Note also that :196's WHEN OTHER does not blank the two cursor fields the way the scan's own WHEN OTHER at :179-181 would have, so CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SEL-FLG stays 'X' and CDEMO-CT00-TRN-SELECTED keeps 0000000000000022 even though TRNID02O now displays 0000000000000002 - the scan ran before the page was painted. INITIALIZE-TRAN-DATA at :450-505 blanks only the four data items of each row and never the selection cell, so the 'X' is redisplayed as well. COTRN00C LISTS transactions from the TRANSACT file, although rule R1 requires the migrated class to be called TransactionMenuController: the name comes from the prompt and every expectation here from the source. STATICALLY DERIVED - never captured from a running COBOL program. The expectations were read out of app/cbl/COTRN00C.cbl paragraph by paragraph and cross-checked against the 350-byte layout in app/cpy/CVTRA05Y.cpy, the symbolic-map widths in app/cpy-bms/COTRN00.CPY, the DFHMDF definitions in app/bms/COTRN00.bms and the CT00 binding in app/csd/CARDDEMO.CSD (practice B12, risk R-A).",
